@startuml
title Cancel Own Booking — Sequence Diagram

actor Employee
participant "Web Frontend" as Frontend
participant "FastAPI Bookings API" as API
database PostgreSQL
participant "Outbox Publisher" as Publisher
queue RabbitMQ
participant "Email Worker" as Worker
participant "Email Provider\n(SMTP / UniSender Go)" as Email

Employee -> Frontend : Open "My bookings"
Frontend -> API : GET /api/v1/bookings/my\nX-Demo-Role: EMPLOYEE
API -> PostgreSQL : Select employee bookings
PostgreSQL --> API : Booking list
API --> Frontend : 200 OK + bookings

Employee -> Frontend : Confirm cancellation
Frontend -> API : POST /api/v1/bookings/{booking_id}/cancel\nX-Demo-Role: EMPLOYEE
API -> PostgreSQL : Load booking by ID
PostgreSQL --> API : Booking or no result

alt Booking does not exist
    API --> Frontend : 404 BOOKING_NOT_FOUND
else Booking belongs to another user
    API --> Frontend : 403 FORBIDDEN
else Booking is not ACTIVE
    API --> Frontend : 409 BOOKING_NOT_ACTIVE
else Less than 30 minutes remain
    API --> Frontend : 409 BOOKING_CANCELLATION_TOO_LATE
else Cancellation is allowed
    API -> PostgreSQL : In one transaction:\nset status = CANCELLED;\nset cancelled_at, cancelled_by, updated_at;\ninsert BookingCancelled outbox event (PENDING)
    PostgreSQL --> API : Commit successful

    alt Serverless mode: NOTIFICATION_DELIVERY=unisender_api
        API -> Email : Send BookingCancelled email [HTTPS]
        Email --> API : Delivery result
        note right of API
          An email failure is logged and does not
          roll back the committed cancellation.
        end note
    else Asynchronous RabbitMQ mode
        API -> API : Direct sender is skipped
    end

    API --> Frontend : 200 OK + cancelled booking
    Frontend --> Employee : Show cancellation success
end

opt Asynchronous notification processing
    Publisher -> PostgreSQL : Read PENDING outbox event
    PostgreSQL --> Publisher : BookingCancelled event
    Publisher -> RabbitMQ : Publish booking.cancelled
    Publisher -> PostgreSQL : Mark event PUBLISHED
    RabbitMQ -> Worker : Deliver BookingCancelled
    Worker -> PostgreSQL : Load user, room and office context
    PostgreSQL --> Worker : Notification context
    Worker -> Email : Send cancellation email [SMTP]
    alt Email sent
        Worker -> RabbitMQ : ACK
    else Email failed
        Worker -> RabbitMQ : NACK (requeue=false)\nRoute to DLQ
    end
end

@enduml
